+## Request 25: Polish renderInvoiceText (COMPLETED)
+
+### What was done
+- Enhanced renderInvoiceText(invoice) in src/render.js to show:
+  - Line discounts: Shows "Discount (X%): -€amount" for lines with discountPercent > 0, indented with 2 spaces
+  - Vouchers: Shows "Voucher (code): -€amount" just before the total line (if present)
+  - Due dates: Shows "Due: YYYY-MM-DD" at the end (all invoices have a dueDate due to default NET30 terms)
+  - Paid amounts: Shows "Paid: €amount" summing all payments (if any exist)
+- Display order is preserved: line items → line discounts → VAT → voucher → total → due date → paid amount
+- Updated test/render.test.js with 13 comprehensive new tests:
+  - Line discount display (with/without, multiple lines, decimal percentages)
+  - Voucher display (with/without)
+  - Due date display (always present due to default NET30 terms)
+  - Paid amount display (single/multiple payments)
+  - Indentation of line discounts
+  - Full invoice with all features
+  - Display order verification
+- Test status: All 370 tests passing (including 13 new render tests)
+
+### Design
+- Line discounts indented with 2 spaces to show they're part of the line item
+- Voucher displayed after VAT, just before total, so customer sees the deduction clearly
+- Due date always shown (since all invoices get default NET30 terms)
+- Paid amount sums all recorded payments for transparency
+- Order follows logical flow: charges → discounts → taxes → deductions → total → timeline → payment status
+
+### Display Format
+```
+INV-2026-0001
+Customer Name
+5 x Product Name @ €85.00 = €425.00
+  Discount (10%): -€42.50
+VAT: €89.25
+Voucher (CODE): -€25.00
+Total: €447.75
+Due: 2026-11-06
+Paid: €200.00
+```
+
 ## Next Steps
 - Available for future invoice features (persistence, API endpoints, etc.)
